### 5. Database schema – where the emails land

**File**: `apps/web/prisma/schema.prisma`

```path/to/apps/web/prisma/schema.prisma#L679-701
model EmailMessage {
  id              String   @id @default(cuid())
  createdAt       DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt       DateTime @updatedAt
  threadId        String
  messageId       String
  date            DateTime   // actual e‑mail sent/received time
  from            String
  fromName        String?
  fromDomain      String
  to              String
  unsubscribeLink String?
  read            Boolean
  sent            Boolean
  draft           Boolean
  inbox           Boolean

  emailAccountId  String
  emailAccount    EmailAccount @relation(fields: [emailAccountId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  @@unique([emailAccountId, threadId, messageId])
  @@index([emailAccountId, threadId])
  @@index([emailAccountId, date])
  @@index([emailAccountId, from])
}
```

* The **unique composite index** guarantees idempotent inserts (`skipDuplicates` in `createMany`).
* Various indexes (`date`, `from`, `threadId`) make the analytics queries fast.

