Below is a quick‑run‑through of what would happen if you triggered the **“load email stats”** workflow from the UI (the `StatLoaderProvider` you just saw).

| Step | Action | Code that does it |
|------|--------|-------------------|
| **1️⃣  UI call** | A component (e.g. `<LoadStats loadBefore={true} …/>`) mounts and runs `onLoad`. | `StatLoaderProvider.tsx → onLoad → statLoader.loadStats()` |
| **2️⃣  Server‑action invoke** | `loadEmailStatsAction(emailAccountId, { loadBefore })` is called. | `StatLoaderProvider.tsx → loadEmailStatsAction` |
| **3️⃣  Resolve provider** | Looks up the `EmailAccount` row, reads the stored provider (`google` or `microsoft`) and creates the concrete provider (`GmailProvider` or `OutlookProvider`). | `utils/actions/stats.ts → createEmailProvider` |
| **4️⃣  Determine pagination anchors** | Queries the DB for the newest (and optionally the oldest) stored `EmailMessage` rows to know where to start. | `loadEmails → prisma.emailMessage.findFirst` |
| **5️⃣  Fetch a page of metadata** | Calls `provider.getMessagesWithPagination({ after, before, maxResults, pageToken })`. <br> – **Gmail** builds a search string with `before:` / `after:` timestamps. <br> – **Outlook** builds OData date filters (`receivedDateTime lt/gt`). | `utils/email/google.ts` & `utils/email/microsoft.ts` |
| **6️⃣  Pull full payloads** | Once a page of IDs is received, the code asks the provider for the full RFC822 bodies in one batch request (`provider.getMessagesBatch`). | `saveBatch → emailProvider.getMessagesBatch` |
| **7️⃣  Transform → DB rows** | For each `ParsedMessage` the code extracts: <br> • `threadId`, `messageId` <br> • `from`, `fromName`, `fromDomain` <br> • `to` <br> • `date` (converted from Gmail’s `internalDate`) <br> • Unsubscribe link (HTML parsing) <br> • Flags: `read`, `sent`, `draft`, `inbox` | `saveBatch → mapping logic` |
| **8️⃣  Bulk insert** | Inserts the rows with `prisma.emailMessage.createMany({ skipDuplicates:true })`. The unique composite index `(emailAccountId, threadId, messageId)` prevents duplicate entries. | `saveBatch → prisma.emailMessage.createMany` |
| **9️⃣  Loop** | The function repeats steps 5‑8 until: <br> – No more pages (`nextPageToken` absent) **or** <br> – The page returned fewer than `PAGE_SIZE` messages **or** <br> – The hard‑coded `MAX_PAGES` (50) limit is hit. | `loadEmails` while‑loops (forward & backward) |
| **🔔  UI feedback** | When `loadStats` finishes, the provider shows a toast: “Stats loaded!” (or an error toast). | `StatLoaderProvider.tsx → toastSuccess / toastError` |

