✅ What you need to run the **core email‑fetch‑and‑store** workflow on a self‑hosted instance

Below is a concise checklist that tells you which parts of the codebase are **essential** for pulling messages from Gmail/Outlook and persisting them locally, and which parts are **optional / external‑service‑specific** that you can safely remove or replace if you don’t want to depend on them.

---

### 1️⃣ Core pieces (must stay)

| Piece | Where it lives | What it does |
|------|----------------|--------------|
| **`loadEmailStatsAction`** | `apps/web/utils/actions/stats.ts` | Server‑action that drives the whole “load‑emails” flow. Calls `createEmailProvider` → `loadEmails`. |
| **Email provider factory** | `apps/web/utils/email/provider.ts` | Picks `GmailProvider` or `OutlookProvider` based on the account’s `provider` field. |
| **`GmailProvider.getMessagesWithPagination`** | `apps/web/utils/email/google.ts` (lines ≈ 812‑836) | Builds Gmail search string (including `before:`/`after:` timestamps), calls `utils/gmail/message#getMessages`, then resolves each ID to a full `ParsedMessage`. |
| **`OutlookProvider.getMessagesWithPagination`** | `apps/web/utils/email/microsoft.ts` (lines ≈ 713‑740) | Splits free‑text query from OData date filters, calls `utils/outlook/message#queryBatchMessages`. |
| **`loadEmails` / `saveBatch`** | Same file as the action | ‑ Paginate forward (newer) and optionally backward (older) relative to the newest/oldest row stored in the DB. <br>‑ Transform each `ParsedMessage` into an `EmailMessage` payload (extract sender, date, unsubscribe link, label flags). <br>‑ Bulk‑insert via `prisma.emailMessage.createMany({ skipDuplicates:true })`. |
| **Prisma schema for `EmailMessage`** | `apps/web/prisma/schema.prisma` (lines ≈ 679‑703) | Stores message‑level data locally (threadId, messageId, from, to, date, flags, unsubscribe link). The unique constraint `(emailAccountId, threadId, messageId)` guarantees idempotency. |
| **OAuth token refresh helpers** | `utils/account.ts` (`getGmailClientForEmail`, `getOutlookClientForEmail`) | Refreshes the user’s access token and returns a ready‑to‑use API client. |
| **Database migrations** | `prisma` folder | Run `npx prisma migrate dev` after cloning – creates `EmailMessage` table and all other required tables. |

> **Bottom line** – if you keep the files above, the “fetch‑and‑store” workflow works unchanged, regardless of any UI, analytics, or paid‑tier code.

