### 2️⃣ External services that are **optional** (you can strip them out)

| Service | Where it’s used | What you can do |
|--------|----------------|-----------------|
| **Upstash /QStash** – background queue for heavy jobs (clean‑up, bulk archive, digest, scheduled actions). | Many `api/*/watch/*`, `api/clean/*`, `api/resend/*`, `utils/upstash.ts`. There are *fallback* routes that simply reject the request when `env.QSTASH_TOKEN` is missing. | • Set `QSTASH_TOKEN` = empty → the fallback routes (`/api/*/batch/simple`) will automatically return a 400/401 and **won’t crash**. <br>• If you prefer a different queue (BullMQ, Sidekiq, cron), replace the helper `publishToQstash` / `publishToQstashQueue` with your own implementation. |
| **PostHog** – analytics tracking (`posthog.capture(...)`). | UI hooks (`hooks/useAnalytics.ts`, `bulk‑unsubscribe/hooks.ts`, feature‑flag hooks). | • Remove the `posthog` import and all `posthog.capture` calls – the app will still function. <br>• If you still want analytics, just provide a dummy `PostHog` object that implements `.capture()`. |
| **Stripe** – premium subscription management (billing, tier gating). | `app/api/stripe/*`, `app/api/premium/*`, several queries that filter on `stripeSubscriptionStatus`. | • Delete the `stripe` folder (`apps/web/ee` or `apps/web/app/api/stripe/*`). <br>• Remove the `stripe`‑related fields from `User.premium` in the Prisma schema if you don’t need them, then run `prisma migrate dev`. <br>• If you want to keep the DB columns for future use, just leave them – the code will simply never hit those routes. |
| **Resend** – transactional email service for digest / summary emails. | `app/api/resend/*`, `utils/resend` imports, env var `RESEND_FROM_EMAIL`. | • Disable the digest/summary CRON jobs (`/api/resend/digest/all`, `/api/resend/summary/all`) by removing the corresponding `cron` entries or setting `hasCronSecret` to `false`. <br>• If you still want email sending, swap `@inboxzero/resend` with any SMTP / Nodemailer wrapper. |
| **LemonSqueezy** – alternative subscription provider (rarely used). | Checks in `watch/*` queries (`lemonSqueezyRenewsAt`). | Same approach as Stripe – either keep the column or drop it. |
| **OpenAI / Claude** – AI‑assisted features (drafts, summarization, persona generation). | `utils/ai/*`, calls to `processHistoryForUser`, `aiSummarizeEmailForDigest`, etc. | These are **purely optional** for the email‑store workflow; you can comment out the import of the AI client and any `ai*` functions that you don’t need. The rest of the system (fetch, store, stats) remains unaffected. |

> **Why it works:** All background‑job endpoints are wrapped with `verifySignatureAppRouter` (Upstash QStash). The code explicitly checks `if (env.QSTASH_TOKEN) … else …` and provides a **fallback** that returns an error, so simply omitting the token disables the queue without breaking the API.

